        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: handle Claude Education quota gaps",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- treat Claude subscription notices without numeric session quota fields as an unavailable quota contract, not a red provider failure\n- suppress refresh cancellation as control flow and preserve valid provider state\n- keep Claude-local cost/token history eligible for menus and widgets; compact widgets fall back to that local value when quota rows are absent\n- document the Education/organization-managed subscription boundary without deriving quota percentages from spend or tokens\n\nThe Claude CLI subscription notice does not provide numeric session or weekly quota fields, so CodexBar cannot truthfully manufacture quota percentages. This change keeps the useful local history visible and reports quota as unavailable instead.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `make check`\n- `make test`\n- focused regression suite for subscription-only parsing, cancellation, menu fallback, provider isolation, token-only widget snapshots, and compact-widget presentation\n- `./Scripts/package_app.sh`\n- fresh packaged app launch; exact binary path verified, status item visibly present, in-bounds Peekaboo menu interaction, app remained running without a surfaced cancellation error\n- autoreview clean after the accepted compact-widget finding was fixed\n\nFixes #1808\n",
